WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.819
Pixar just released the next sneak peek at
Incredibles 2 and hidden in the new footage

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:08.920
are some cool details and easter eggs you
might have missed.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.969
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm delving into the new Incredibles

00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:17.440
2 trailer for Pixar easter eggs, superhero
references and a possible villain we haven't

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.440
yet met.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.210
If you're new here, I do lots of Pixar and
superhero movie videos, so subscribe to my

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.660
channel to get everything as soon as I post
it.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:31.370
Plus, I've got a new Pixar giveaway for all
my subscribers later in this video!

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.140
"Superheroes are illegal."

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.100
"We wanna fight bad guys!"

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.100
"Ajubadibaja!"

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.100
"It defines who I am!"

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.550
"We're not saying you have... what?!"

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.380
If like Mr Incredible, you're wondering where
this line came from, well, it seems to be

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.400
a cool reference to Batman Begins.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.690
"It's not who I am underneath, but what I
do ... that defines me."

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:55.210
I love that Pixar are obviously continuing
to have fun with superhero lore and putting

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.780
their own spin on lines from Christopher Nolan's
Batman trilogy.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.750
Also in this scene is a regular, but less
well-known, Pixar easter egg which is a very

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.649
specific Chinese take-out container design.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:11.039
This same style of food box has appeared four
times previously in Pixar movies.

00:01:11.039 --> 00:01:15.360
The first time was in A Bug's Life where it
was called the "Chinese Cabinet of Metamorphosis"

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.189
by Manny who used it for his circus act.

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:30.609
"From the most mysterious regions of uncharted
Asia, I give you the Chinese Cabinet Of Metamorphosis!"

00:01:30.609 --> 00:01:34.950
Other places it's appeared in Pixar movies
include in the Pizza Planet Truck in Toy Story

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:40.469
2, in Linguini's apartment in Ratatouille,
and, most recently, in Inside Out where, like

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:44.810
the Incredibles family, Riley and her family
also sat down for a dinner of Chinese takeout.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.890
"Help me bring supers back into the sunlight."

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.869
"We need Elastigirl!"

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:50.200
"Bye sweetie!"

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.170
"I'll watch the kids, no problem."

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:59.489
OK, so here we get our first look at Winston
Deavor and his Devtech organisation and he's

00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:03.060
making it clear he wants to hire Elastigirl
for his own missions.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:08.270
Now, if we jump back a moment to this shot
at the Municiberg airport, there's Elastigirl

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:12.600
arriving on her motorbike, but look really
carefully and you'll notice there's another

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.610
figure standing next to Winston Deavor.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:21.810
I wonder if that could be his sister Evelyn,
who you can gather from her name – Evelyn

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:26.920
Deavor – sounds like she's probably going
to have a villainous role in the movie.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:30.790
We also get to see that Elastigirl's been
kitted out with a new slick outfit as well

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.900
as a motorbike and they both have an interesting
new logo, which looks like the letters E and

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.590
G of Elastigirl have been combined.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:43.000
And notice that the waterfall that Elastigirl
drives out of is a call-back to Syndrome's

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.750
lava waterfall which also worked as a hidden
opening in the first Incredibles movie.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.410
On the surface, the math joke seems it's probably
a jab at the US Common Core math standard

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.260
and the criticism it's come under from parents.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.360
"That's not the way you're supposed to do
it Dad."

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.530
"They want us to do it this..."

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.480
"I don't know that way!

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.060
Why would they change math?!"

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.060
"Math is math!"

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.060
"It's OK Dad!"

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.060
"Math is math!"

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.350
However, given the book Dash holds up is called
"New Math for Life", this might actually also

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.960
be a reference to the "New Math" syllabus
which was introduced in the 1960s in the US

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.620
and some European countries as an attempt
to improve mathematical skills and interest

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.670
in science during the Cold War.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:26.650
Additionally, this fits in with the [19]60s-esque
setting of the Incredibles movies.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.540
We also get a glimpse of Jack-Jack literally
turning into a little monster again, as he

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.910
did when he defended himself against Syndrome
at the end of the first film.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.900
"But I can't keep giving him cookies!"

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.900
"Wow!"

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.900
"No biting the Daddy!"

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.730
The trailer's cut together pretty quickly,
but it looks like Jack-Jack gets this specific

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:49.790
power when he's angry, and it seems here it's
because Mr Incredible won't give him any more

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:50.790
cookies.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:56.010
It was great to see Edna Mode back and, judging
by the look of Mr Incredible, I think he'll

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.430
be turning to her for help after becoming
exhausted trying to look after Jack-Jack.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.370
As she did for Elastigirl in the first movie,
I'm sure this time she'll be offering him

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.440
some of her signature brand of advice!

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.709
"What are you talking about?"

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:09.709
"Huh?"

00:04:09.709 --> 00:04:11.230
"You are Elastigirl!"

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.380
"My god, pull yourself together!"

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.889
And I wonder if she'll also be designing him
or Jack-Jack a new costume?

00:04:18.889 --> 00:04:21.489
But no capes, of course, dahling!

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:23.889
"Something classic, like Dyna Guy!"

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:26.009
"Oh, he had a great look!"

00:04:26.009 --> 00:04:27.779
"The cape and the boots!"

00:04:27.779 --> 00:04:28.779
"No capes!"

